Hi everyone,
Although the following question is strictly speaking not on S-plus I dare to
pose it here since many people using this facility would have the knowledge
to answer it. 

Suppose that there is an assay for which the value is not detectable when it
drops under 9. Teh median of the assay is 15 , the largest value is 80 the
75-th percentile is 30. Up to now in the literature all the values under 9
were considered exactly=9. This way of looking of teh data overestimates the
mean and underestimates the standard deviation. 
My question is:
Is tere a way to deal with this problem?
Can these values be imputed ?
I would be grateful for any references.
Thank you.

