Which version of S-PLUS?

[example clipped: a test of apply, only]

On my 64Mb Solaris 2.6 box (the Q was about Solaris not Linux) my results
are quite different: R is about twice as fast as S-PLUS 5 on your example
but uses much more memory: S-PLUS 3.4 was about 1.5x faster again. There is
no S-PLUS 3.x on Linux to compare.

In earlier versions of S-PLUS 5 apply() was slower than for(). This should
come as no surprise: read what John Chambers says about it in the Green
Book (shipped with S-PLUS 5).

Benchmarking is a slippery game: one thing I learnt many years ago was to
use real problems of realistic size. Another (more recently) was that the
optimal code in S-PLUS 3.x, S-PLUS 5.x and R may not be the same.

The bootstrapping examples in the forthcoming V&R3 all work satisfactorily
on all three S-like systems.

