Subject: [S] Rearranging Columns in a Dataframe
Message-ID: <4.1.19990410140208.009bbe20@pop4.ibm.net>

I have a dataframe with 87 columns (87 variables).  Is there some simple
way to rearrange the columns so that the variables occur in alphabetical
order?  The data are standard anthropometric data, cited in the literature
typically in ascending alphabetical order.  The original data are in
anatomical order.  If one is trying to replicate results reported by other
researchers who have used a subset of the original data, it is extremely
difficult to "find" the particular variables easily when they appear in a
completely different order in the file than in the published tables.

There is a row.name parameter but there doesn't seem to be a column.name
parameter.  I can do this manually in the GUI, or I can do it by manually
performing the alphabetization using the mapping of variable indices with
variable names.  Both solutions seem pretty inefficient.  I can't find any
way to do this in any other program either, so not finding an easy way in
S-Plus wouldn't surprise me.  On the other hand, *this* group has been
incredibly inventive with solutions so far.  

