> It depends if you have included a nugget effect. If not, kriging is an
> exact interpolator, so prediction at data points is pointless. If you have,
> it should fit a smooth surface, but this is one detail of my
> library(spatial) that was not copied well enough, so predict.krige actually
> fits a smooth surface with spikes.
>
> I think you need to read a good book on spatial statistics or consult a
> local expert: this is not a software question and it is difficult to give
> an answer without knowing how basic your knowledge really is.
