Subject: [S] the General Linear Hypothesis
Message-ID: <199904122015.OAA20266@ulysses.sis.ualberta.ca>

Consider a multivariate linear regression model

        Y = X \Theta + E

where Y is a n by m data matrix
      X a  n by p regressor matrix
      \Theta a p by m matrix of parameters
        to be estimated.
and   E is a n by m error matrix with mean 0 etc.

In the terminology of Mardia Kent and Bibby (1979)
the general linear hypothesis on \Theta may be written

        C \Theta M = D

where C and M represent constraints on the dependent and 
independent variables. This GLH can be tested within
the model by likelihood ratio tests.

Are there any Splus libraries which  

        a) do multivariate regression
        b) support this form of hypothesis testing
        c) support more general constraints
           on \Theta (methods using Kronecker products
           exist).

I've checked the manuals and the statlib cite,
but can find nothing helpful.

