Answers from B. Biggerstaff and N. Robbins:

Essentially you need to re-build your _Prefs directory (likely in
something
like "c:\Program Files\splus45\users\you\_prefs").  So you need to
delete
the _Prefs directory and re-start S-Plus, which will then build one for
you.
(I'm sure there's a particular file in there, but redoing the whole
thing is
easier.)  Any session characteristics you had set, like having the
commands
window on start-up and no object browser on start-up, will have to be
re-set.  It's not a bad idea to set up these session characteristics
like
you want and then save the _Prefs directory in a backup, like
_Prefs.bak,
for just such an occasion as you have now.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

If you move the "_Prefs" folder in your home directory to another
location
where S-PLUS can't find it (to your root "C:\" directory, for example),
then restart S-PLUS, that should restore the default menu and toolbars,
including the links to the help files.

I hope this helps,

