Subject: [S] computing tied ranks
Message-ID: <371472F1.A633BE87@est-econ.uc3m.es>

Hi,

This is for Splus 4.5 on Windows 95.

I am not sure if the following can be considered a bug. It comes up when
computing ranks of differences. Even though some differences are tied,
the "naive" way of computing their ranks does not pick this up.

> x
[1] 2.4 1.3 1.5 0.9
> y
[1] 2.1 0.9 2.0 0.6
> x - y
[1]  0.3  0.4 -0.5  0.3
> rank(x - y)
[1] 2 4 1 3
> rank(c(0.3, 0.4, -0.5, 0.3))
[1] 2.5 4.0 1.0 2.5
> rank(round(10*(x - y)))
[1] 2.5 4.0 1.0 2.5

Is there a more natural way to avoid this "bug" than the quick-and-dirty
method of the last line?

Thanks,
Michael

