As the other user of Mark's utilities that he refered to, I would add my
"testimony" that the utilities have solved for me what is a long
standing weakness of the Splus system.  

The investment in installing and learning Mark's project management
system is more than returned almost immediately in terms of efficiency.
This may be more the case for those of us who works on multiple projects
simultaneously, but I would guess that it is useful for single project
people as well because it allows easy formation of heirarchial
structures that keep related objects and functions grouped.  (And don't
overlook the clever substitute for fix that keeps your formats, and the
even more clever substitute debugger, and various other utilities, like
foodweb which shows which functions are called by which).

But one has to wonder why I would bother to write such a supporting
email; Mark has described his project management software, and you all
can respond or not.  The reason I bothered to write is selfish.  

It seems to me that Mark has simplified and automated the attach and
detach functions in a way that Mathsoft should pay attention to.  If
something like this were incorporated in the Splus package, the system
would be easier to use and I would in the longer term be happier.  So I
write with the specific intention to tell Mathsoft to pay attention.

But don't hold your breath for Mathsoft (they've ignored the problem for
as long as I've been using their product).  Instead, let out your breath
and ask Mark for a copy.

Tim Smith

