Ulric -

Last Thursday I spent nearly a full day trying to figure this out. It was a
special kind of pain since For() didn't report any error messages, it just
didn't do any work for me. The fix on my desktop was to simplify the
.First.lib function in the hmisc library, which is attached in my .First
function [removing the locate.menu.item() call there was what fixed the
problem]. On my laptop the fix was to make sure the environmental variable
SHOME was set (even though the readme.txt says SHOME is ignored and S_HOME
is now used by SPlus 4.5). Basically, run SQPE at the DOS prompt and make
sure you're not getting any error messages there. Once you get that working
For() should work.

Still, using For() causes the warning message:

Warning messages:
  Unable to create summary in summary file d:\temp\_data/__sum4.txt. in:
assign.default(".Steps", steps, w = 1, immediate = T)

to start coming up. Deleting __sum4i.txt, __sum4.txt and __sum4.tx_ in the
corresponding _data directory gets rid of the error message, but don't
bother until you're done using For() for a while. Using For() will make the
warning come right back.

Ed
callahan at envstat.com

