Subject: [S] Dumb S History Question
Message-ID: <4.1.19990421090137.0098c2a0@pop4.ibm.net>

Many of the S (S-Plus) functions have an na.action=na.fail default
argument.  While using the var() and cor() function, I noted that these
functions (and probably others) have an na.method="fail" default argument.
In the first instance, changing the default requires na.action=na.omit (for
example), while in the second cases, changing the default requires
na.method="omit".

Are these differences intentional (e.g. to prevent earlier versions of code
from braking) or are these simply historical holdovers that have not been
cleaned up in newer versions of S-Plus?  

I'm sure there is some interesting (or perhaps boring) history here.  I'd
be curious why there isn't more consistency in this type of default argument.

