From jhrockwe at uop.com  Wed Apr 21 17:30:21 1999
From: jhrockwe at uop.com (Rockwell, James)
Date: Wed, 21 Apr 1999 12:30:21 -0500
Subject: [S] Creating MS PowerStation 4.0 Fortran DLL and running on S-Plus 4. 5
Message-ID: <09A078107652D211A83700805F575E0537A81D@DPLMAIL6.internal.uop.com>

Previous e-mail had error in S+ dll.load---corrected below.

I have Splus 4.5 for Windows 95 (release 2), and MS Fortran Power Station
4.0, and I want to be able to load dll's into S-Plus.
(My configuration is Pentium 200, 128Mb RAM, W95) Has someone been able to
to do this using the above software
combination? I have tried different options for creating the .dll file, but
I always get error codes when using dll.load in S-Plus. 

I will summarize results.

Thanks to Jun Zhai and Tim Smith I finally got a Fortran dll generated and
running on S+ as shown below:

C       File> New> Project Workspace> Dynamic Link Library 
C                                       + Name: FORTDLLEG > Create
C       File> New> Text file>  Write Fortran code shown below
C       File> Save As> SUMPROD.for
C       Build> Compile> SUMPROD.for
C       Build> Build FORTDLLEG.dll
C       
C       Use dumpkin -exports FORTDLLEQ.dll to see symbol name(s)

C
C       Copy FORTDLLEQ.dll to C:\SPLUS\CMD directory
C
C       S+ Functions:
C
C       SumProddll.load<- function()
C       {
C        dll.load("FORTDLLEQ.dll","SUMPROD")
C       }
C       
C       f.SumProd<- function()
C       {
C        N<-3
C        X<-1:3
C        Y<-30:32
C        R<-0
C        return(.Fortran(""SUMPROD",as.integer(N),as.double(X),as.double(Y),
C                as.double(R))
C       }
C
      SUBROUTINE SUMPROD(NTERM, X, Y, SUM) 
        !MS$ATTRIBUTES DLLEXPORT,ALIAS:'SUMPROD'::SUMPROD
        INTEGER*4 NTERM, I 
        REAL*8 X(NTERM), Y(NTERM), SUM
        SUM=0
        DO 10 I= 1, NTERM       
   10   SUM=SUM+X(I)*Y(I)
        END     SUBROUTINE SUMPROD

Many Thanks,

Jim Rockwell
